Fixes #62239

With verbatimModuleSyntax on, tsc kept an empty `{}` after a default import when all the named imports were type-only:

```ts
import A, { type T } from "./a";
// before: import A, {} from "./a";
// after:  import A from "./a";
```

The default binding keeps the import, so the braces do nothing there. Imports without a default binding still emit `import {} from "./a"`, and a `{}` you write in the source stays. 6.0 emits the braces too, and this PR changes that. Ryan [approved](https://github.com/microsoft/TypeScript/pull/62349#pullrequestreview-3273307924) the same change for the old codebase in #62349 before the bot closed it during the 6.0 freeze.

I wrote this change with Claude Code. I chose this issue, read and understand the change, and will handle review feedback myself.
